  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans, as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice. \rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than seven residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate surroundings \r",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.",
    "The refuse and recycling storage hereby approved on drawing no. P07 shall be provided in accordance with the approved details prior to occupation of the development hereby approved and thereafter maintained unless otherwise in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Borough's waste reduction targets.",
    "Notwithstanding the details shown on drawing P07, the development shall not be occupied until details of the required 7 long-stay cycle parking spaces have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \rThese details should demonstrate: \rLocation: Near entrances or main access, minimum 1.2m wide access route \rDesign: Stands \rSecurity: Secure, overlooked, well-lit \rCoverage: Covered \rAccessibility: Step-free, no obstructions \r\rThe approved bicycle parking shall be provided prior to occupation and thereafter permanently retained. \r\rReason: To ensure that sufficient provision at all times so that the development does not prejudice the free flow of traffic or the conditions of general safety along the adjacent highway, or the amenities and convenience of existing local residents.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture those specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The outbuilding shall not be occupied at any time other than for purposes ancillary to the residential use of the existing dwelling and shall not be used as an independent dwelling at any time.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development complies with adopted standards, does not impact on neighbouring amenity, and that it is in character with the form of development in the locality, in accordance with relevant adopted planning policies of the Enfield Local Plan.\r"
  ],
